{% set f = rules.fate %}
{% set trim = rules.context.budget_trim_min_chars %}
{% set tasks %}
=== TASKS ===
{% include "shared/verdict_criteria.md.j2" %}

TASK 2, Naming: give every record born of the world's own course a real name fitting the naming language, a subtype, a description and an image prompt. For those marked "name kept" the name is already fixed: keep that name EXACTLY, call the record by it in the description, and only write the subtype, description and prompt. The description must describe the record ITSELF. {% include "shared/no_numbers_clause.md.j2" %}

TASK 3: Name the prophecies that came true; reward the sons who advanced the stories.
TASK 4, Facts: extract short, definite facts from the creations you accepted and the records you named. If a new creation violates the "Canon facts" listed in the details, give "fix".
TASK 5, Words: a few new words that enter the languages from this age's events (language_id, word, meaning, origin).
TASK 6, Stories: stories must reach an end. In this age, close AT LEAST {{ min_close }} open stories{% if close_candidates %}; one of them MUST be from the priority candidates (stretched too long or stagnant) and must be written in the resolved_story field: {% for candidate in close_candidates %}story#{{ candidate }}{% if not loop.last %}, {% endif %}{% endfor %}. Closing the easiest story (young, never advanced) is not resolving{% endif %}. The closing must be concrete: a consequence born of this age's events or of the creations that advanced it; if nobody touched it, tell plainly how it ended without anyone acting on it. Before closing, look: if an event or record of this age concretely advanced an open story (even if nobody gave story_id), write it in advanced_stories (at most {{ f.thread_advance_cap }}); close a never-advanced story only if it has truly lapsed, and say plainly that it lapsed. Closing a young story that never advanced as "nothing happened" is FORBIDDEN (only those stagnant for {{ f.zero_progress_close_epochs | several("age", "ages") }} may close as lapsed); first bring the most advanced candidates to a concrete end. A closing may start something new where this age's events lead to it. Open at most {{ new_max }} new stories; each must rest on a concrete question or change born this age and be bound to specific entities. A new story is born in ONE world: bind records of two worlds only if a concrete contact shown in the data links them and the story's text names that contact.
{% include "shared/lore_language.md.j2" %} {% include "shared/_harm_narration.md.j2" %}

{% endset %}
